; Example zone file for importing into Cloudflare (DNS -> Records -> Import).
; Replace example.com and the documentation addresses with your own, keep the
; DNS-only (grey cloud) setting for the VPN hostname: proxying it would break
; the VPN, because Cloudflare only proxies HTTP(S).
;
; The VPN hostname is the one casavpn-ddns keeps up to date; the address below
; is a placeholder it will overwrite. Keep the TTL at 60 so a new address
; reaches the clients within a minute (Cloudflare's "Auto" is 300 seconds).
$ORIGIN example.com.
$TTL 3600

; web (if you have one)
@        3600 IN A     203.0.113.40
www      3600 IN CNAME example.com.

; mail (replace with your provider's records, or delete)
@        3600 IN MX    10 mx1.mail.example.net.
@        3600 IN MX    10 mx2.mail.example.net.
@        3600 IN TXT   "v=spf1 include:mail.example.net ~all"

; the VPN: DNS only, short TTL, IPv4 only (no AAAA: the home router forwards v4)
vpn        60 IN A     198.51.100.10
